WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.390
- So it looks like Alex Jones

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.290
is going to have to pay

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.530
a huge amount of money

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.210
to the parents of the children

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.470
that were killed in the
Sandy Hook Massacre.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:08.520
And this isn't a case

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.070
that it wasn't at all clear

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.450
that Alex Jones was going to lose.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.700
So how did he snatch defeat

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.630
from the jaws of victory?

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.870
Well, you have to hand it to him,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:18.703
he just achieved something

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:20.870
that's so rare in Texas legal circles,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:21.840
that one lawyer called it

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.690
a unicorn in the law.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.523
One lawyer said,

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:25.667
"None of the lawyers I've spoken with

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:26.947
"have ever had this happen,

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:28.317
"but we've never seen such a blatant

00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.647
"disregard for the court's authority

00:00:29.647 --> 00:00:31.220
"the way we have here."

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.230
So what did Jones do in this lawsuit?

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.063
Well, first of all,

00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:35.940
there's four lawsuits

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.420
that were filed by family members

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.440
of three children killed

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.273
in the shooting at

00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:41.080
Sandy Hook Elementary School in 2012.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.650
And despite the verifiable fact

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.100
that six adults and 20 children

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.700
were murdered by a lone gunman,

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.060
Jones has repeatedly accused

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:47.910
Sandy Hook families

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.175
of being crisis actors,

00:00:49.175 --> 00:00:51.028
calling the events at giant hoax

00:00:51.028 --> 00:00:53.020
and a false flag operation.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.330
And several families of victims

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.240
have already sued Jones

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.400
for defamation and won.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.070
In 2019, a court ordered Jones

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.750
to pay court costs and legal fees

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.200
to parents of Sandy Hook victims.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.620
And in the current lawsuits,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.790
Jones has steadfastly refused

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.430
to turn over relevant evidence

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:06.420
to the plaintiffs.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.310
Despite court orders

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.590
that were meant to expedite discovery,

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.280
Jones has declined to provide

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.600
documents and evidence.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.630
But here's the thing about court orders,

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.170
you really don't have the right

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.340
to decline them.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.103
Even if you think the court is wrong.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:23.973
Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:01:23.973 --> 00:01:25.520
It's time to think like a litigator

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.560
because after three years of stonewalling,

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.840
a Texas judge has finally seen enough.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.860
So rather than allowing

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:31.700
the case to go to trial,

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.890
the judge ruled that Jones'

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.110
flagrant bad faith

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.180
and callous disregard
of the court's orders

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.650
has resulted in default judgments.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.450
That means that the judge decided

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.121
that Jones and Infowars
have legal liability.

00:01:43.121 --> 00:01:44.690
The three cases will now proceed

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.090
to trial solely on one issue,

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.710
how much money Jones and Infowars

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.100
have to pay for defamation

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.160
and intentional infliction

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.700
of emotional distress.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.260
So just how did Alex Jones

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.280
lose four lawsuits

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.940
without proceeding to trial?

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.620
Well, let's count the ways.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.110
And to understand why the judge

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.209
issued default judgments,

00:02:01.209 --> 00:02:03.620
we need to know the
basics of these lawsuits.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.760
In 2018, the families of three children

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.737
filed lawsuits in Travis County, Texas

00:02:07.737 --> 00:02:11.300
where Jones and his Infowars
media system is based.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.600
The plaintiffs in these cases

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.987
contend that Jones' false claims

00:02:13.987 --> 00:02:16.540
motivated people to harass
and intimidate them.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.999
For example, Leonard Pozner
and Veronique De La Rosa

00:02:18.999 --> 00:02:21.530
are the parents of
six-year-old Noah Pozner.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.120
One of Jones' viewers, Lucy Richards,

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.010
left voicemails threatening

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.210
to kill Leonard Pozner

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.260
for his alleged role

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.910
in the alleged hoax.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.220
After Pozner convinced YouTube

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.860
to remove one of the Jones' videos,

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.850
Jones then published Pozner's home address

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.070
and showed viewers information

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.500
about Pozner's family members.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.610
The Pozner family has moved seven times

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.680
to avoid harassment from Jones' viewers.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.240
The Pozner-De La Rosa lawsuit

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.250
quoted Jones is saying that

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.170
the school shooting was,

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.467
quote, "A false flag,

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:45.987
"meant to give the
government an opportunity

00:02:45.987 --> 00:02:47.770
"to limit second amendment rights."

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:48.960
And Jones constantly

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.160
tells his viewers and listeners

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.490
that the parents of the slain children

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.000
did not have murdered children.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.667
Quote, "They clearly used actors.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.849
"I mean, they even ended up using

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:58.197
"photos of kids killed in mass shootings

00:02:58.197 --> 00:02:59.847
"here in a fake mass shooting

00:02:59.847 --> 00:03:02.750
"in Turkey or Pakistan," end quote.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.010
Naturally, the parents of children

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.010
killed in Sandy Hook

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.750
took objection to these claims.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.850
Neil Heslin is the father

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.240
of six-year-old Jesse Lewis.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.900
After Joan said Heslin lied about

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.410
holding his dead son in his arms,

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.350
Heslin filed two defamation lawsuits.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.900
Jessie's mother, Scarlett,

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.460
also filed a lawsuit against Jones

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.780
for saying the school shooting was,

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.250
quote, "As phony as a $3 bill."

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.460
Lewis cited numerous statements

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.930
where Jones and his contributors

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.429
implied that the Sandy Hook parents

00:03:25.429 --> 00:03:27.040
were not genuinely grieving

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.390
for their dead children.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.223
By any measure,

00:03:29.223 --> 00:03:31.230
this is gruesomely offensive stuff.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.620
But is it enough to
lose a defamation case?

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.800
Well, before we go
deeper into these cases,

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.216
you should understand some basic facts

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.721
about what we call the discovery process.

00:03:39.721 --> 00:03:41.090
So let's say that you want

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.760
to file a civil lawsuit against someone.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.070
You race down to the courthouse,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:44.903
fill out the paperwork.

00:03:44.903 --> 00:03:47.080
What happens next is not trial.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.189
Before you get your day in court,

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:49.760
all parties get an opportunity

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.200
to get evidence from each other.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.590
This is called discovery

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:53.580
and there are several tools

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.700
that lawyers use in discovery

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:55.690
to gather evidence.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.220
And some information
disclosures are mandatory,

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.240
which prevents the other side

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.812
from hiding relevant evidence.

00:04:00.812 --> 00:04:03.157
In Texas, these required
disclosures are covered by

00:04:03.157 --> 00:04:05.940
the Texas Rule of Civil Procedure 194.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.020
And they include information

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.800
like the name and
address of all witnesses,

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.920
a list or copy of all relevant documents,

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.910
and a description of the legal theories

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.660
and defenses each party may use.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.860
Lawyers may also make requests

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.693
for a production,

00:04:16.693 --> 00:04:17.870
which each side must answer

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:18.920
by producing documents

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.506
and things relevant to the case.

00:04:20.506 --> 00:04:22.380
And these requests must specify

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.573
a reasonable time and date for production.

00:04:24.573 --> 00:04:26.380
Litigants can also ask parties

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.420
to answer written questions

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.580
called interrogatories.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.500
And if you've ever wondered

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.360
what lawyers are actually doing all day,

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.540
this is probably it.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.530
We spend a lot of time

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.220
crafting these discovery requests

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.140
and responding to them,

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:36.973
objecting to them,

00:04:36.973 --> 00:04:38.580
and reviewing answers to them.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.580
Lawyers spend more time

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:40.413
on these activities

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.890
than they do inside the courtroom.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:42.723
And there also be things

00:04:42.723 --> 00:04:43.851
like depositions where witnesses

00:04:43.851 --> 00:04:45.970
must give testimony under oath.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:46.820
And throughout this process,

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.500
all parties negotiate for
limitations on discovery,

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.850
and they try and force the other side

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.210
to answer the requests as written.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.330
There's back and forth between

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.250
the parties and the court.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.990
But eventually, you're going to have

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.860
to answer some of this discovery.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.450
Simply asserting that answering

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.800
discovery requests in general

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.816
is hard work and cumbersome

00:05:03.816 --> 00:05:05.240
is generally not enough

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.970
to get out of doing those
discovery responses.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:08.950
And all of this takes place

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.890
long before the parties ever get to trial,

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.640
where you'll have an adjudication

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.450
of the case on the merits.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.283
In this case,

00:05:15.283 --> 00:05:16.250
the litigants in the defamation case

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.167
all made written discovery requests

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.788
in 2018 and 2019.

00:05:18.788 --> 00:05:20.260
However, in response,

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.570
Jones and his collaborators

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.570
filed motions under

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.720
the Texas Citizens Participation Act,

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.018
known as the TCPA,

00:05:26.018 --> 00:05:28.080
to have the lawsuits dismissed.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.658
The TCPA is Texas' version

00:05:29.658 --> 00:05:31.210
of an anti-SLAPP statute,

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.160
which is meant to be
constitutional safeguard

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.010
protecting the rights
of persons to petition

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.880
to speak freely, associate freely,

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.400
and otherwise participate in government

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.230
to the maximum extent permitted by law.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.240
And at the same time,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.310
protects the rights of persons

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.990
to file meritorious lawsuits

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.400
for demonstrable injury.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.550
SLAPPs are shorthand

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.940
for Strategic Lawsuits
Against Public Participation.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.566
Generally, lawsuits trying
to stifle free speech.

00:05:51.566 --> 00:05:53.120
And anti-SLAPP laws

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.110
are generally a good thing

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.480
for freedom of speech.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.920
They are intended to prevent people

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.610
from using courts to intimidate people

00:05:58.610 --> 00:05:59.825
who are simply exercising

00:05:59.825 --> 00:06:01.381
their free speech rights.

00:06:01.381 --> 00:06:03.370
Media groups and individual journalists

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.720
can use an anti-SLAPP statute

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.553
to protect themselves

00:06:05.553 --> 00:06:07.270
from baseless legal threats.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.120
And interestingly, while
former President Trump

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.012
has been known to file

00:06:10.012 --> 00:06:11.893
a meritless lawsuit or two

00:06:11.893 --> 00:06:15.080
and had anti-SLAPP laws used against him,

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.000
former President Trump

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.920
also used an anti-SLAPP law in his favor

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.610
to get attorney's fees
back from Stormy Daniels

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.443
when the court ruled

00:06:22.443 --> 00:06:24.190
that the Stormy Daniels lawsuit

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.930
was meritless and infringed

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.170
on former President Trump's

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.180
right to free speech.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.013
In this case,

00:06:30.013 --> 00:06:31.842
the Texas anti-SLAPP law, the TCPA,

00:06:31.842 --> 00:06:33.890
was initially criticized

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.160
for being so broad

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.120
that it allowed defendants

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.980
to dismiss too many types of cases,

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.080
including attorney discipline proceedings

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.150
and employment law matters,

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.374
where the issue wasn't
really about free speech.

00:06:43.374 --> 00:06:44.600
But in 2019,

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.640
the Texas legislature

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:47.160
narrowed the scope of the law,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.130
hoping to confine it

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.660
to cases involving the First Amendment.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.440
And the TCPA now provides
litigants like Jones

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:54.690
with an early opportunity

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.230
to move to dismiss a lawsuit

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.570
that infringes on his
First Amendment rights.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.848
And if successful,

00:07:00.848 --> 00:07:02.930
that person can then receive

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.301
an award of attorney's fees.

00:07:04.301 --> 00:07:06.710
So Jones and Infowars had a right

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.390
to file a TCPA motion

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.378
and they did so for all four of the cases.

00:07:10.378 --> 00:07:12.450
The trial judge stayed the proceedings

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.870
while Jones fought for

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.040
his First Amendment rights.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.280
And so far, there's nothing improper

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:17.220
about any of that.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.330
Jones has as many First Amendment rights

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.163
as anyone else.

00:07:20.163 --> 00:07:21.710
And we might not like what he has to say,

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.020
but that's why the First Amendment exists.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:24.981
To protect people

00:07:24.981 --> 00:07:26.670
and their right to say

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.162
what they want to say.

00:07:28.162 --> 00:07:29.740
But Jones has always maintained

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:30.681
that he had a First Amendment right

00:07:30.681 --> 00:07:33.360
to report about the Sandy Hook Massacre.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.810
But his own statements given under oath

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.980
have undermined his defense to defamation.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.980
Jones first got himself into hot water

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:39.890
during his deposition

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.461
in one of the other Sandy Hook cases.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.680
During that deposition,

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.210
lawyers played damning clips

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.310
of Jones on his TV show

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.110
where he was mocking parents,

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:47.943
pretending to cry,

00:07:47.943 --> 00:07:48.776
. parents.

00:07:49.829 --> 00:07:51.530
- And then you've got parents laughing,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.790
going, "Hahaha,"

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:54.185
and then they walk over
to the camera and go...

00:07:54.185 --> 00:07:55.600
(intense crying)

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.670
- In response to the clips,

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:57.840
Jones admitted under oath

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.300
that his statements were false.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.220
Jones said the media traumatized him

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.053
because they were all

00:08:02.053 --> 00:08:03.420
such great big liars.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.530
And the big old media,

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:06.950
therefore, caused Jones
to suffer from a psychosis

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.000
where he simply made things up

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.720
about these families and their children.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:10.553
As you can imagine,

00:08:10.553 --> 00:08:11.386
these kinds of admissions

00:08:11.386 --> 00:08:13.650
hurt Jones in all the defamation cases

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.010
filed by the Sandy Hook families

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.180
and made it easier for them

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.440
to prove intentional infliction

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.841
of emotional distress.

00:08:18.841 --> 00:08:20.410
Jones argued that he had a right

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.243
to ask questions

00:08:21.243 --> 00:08:22.180
and that he relied on evidence

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.320
he found online through news reports.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.457
Quote, "They staged Sandy Hook.

00:08:25.457 --> 00:08:26.677
"The evidence is just overwhelming,

00:08:26.677 --> 00:08:28.027
"and that's why I'm so desperate

00:08:28.027 --> 00:08:28.860
"and freaked out,"

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.790
said Jones in 2013.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:31.710
And his argument was that,

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:32.670
as a news organization,

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:33.503
he and his staff

00:08:33.503 --> 00:08:34.880
had the right to ask questions, speculate

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.548
and rely on what others were reporting

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:38.952
in formulating their own opinions

00:08:38.952 --> 00:08:41.090
in addition to doing their own reporting.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.410
And members of the media

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:44.542
are generally allowed to do just that.

00:08:44.542 --> 00:08:45.820
Of course, a lot of these claims

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.010
were undermined by some

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.598
damning deposition testimony.

00:08:48.598 --> 00:08:50.329
And during the litigation
of these motions,

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.670
Jones admitted that all of

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.700
the factual allegations

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:53.930
in the plaintiff's pleadings were true,

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.710
which isn't really unusual.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.160
In a defamation case,

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.440
often you know what statements

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.230
are being made by both parties.

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:03.660
So it's not unusual for a defendant

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.757
to necessarily agree

00:09:05.757 --> 00:09:07.650
with the factual allegations of

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.720
the plaintiff's pleadings.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.010
It's just that they disagreed

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.020
that they rise to the level

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.360
of a defamatory statement.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.193
And not surprisingly,

00:09:13.193 --> 00:09:14.590
Jones argued that all of his statements

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:15.740
were constitutionally protected

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:16.948
expressions of opinion,

00:09:16.948 --> 00:09:18.850
rather than statements of fact.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:19.970
And under Texas law,

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.560
courts must consider the following factors

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.610
in determining whether a statement

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.810
is one of opinion or fact.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.160
One, the statement must
be provable as false,

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:27.610
at least where public official

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:29.650
or public figure plaintiffs are involved.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:31.030
Two, the constitutional protection

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.290
is afforded to statements

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.650
that cannot reasonably

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.560
be interpreted as stating actual facts

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:36.456
in order to assure that

00:09:36.456 --> 00:09:37.629
the public debate

00:09:37.629 --> 00:09:39.070
will not suffer for lack

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.350
of imaginative expression

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.920
or rhetorical hyperbole.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.315
Or three, where the standard of opinion

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:45.020
on a matter of public concern

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.180
reasonably implies false

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.235
and defamatory facts

00:09:47.235 --> 00:09:49.710
regarding public figures or officials.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.900
Those individuals must show

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:51.733
that such statements

00:09:51.733 --> 00:09:52.780
were made with knowledge

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.070
of their false implications

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.120
or with reckless disregard for the truth.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.490
And four, the statements must be given,

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.900
quote, "enhanced appellate review"

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.410
to ensure that these determinations

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.243
are made in a manner

00:10:01.243 --> 00:10:02.570
that does not constitute

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:04.399
a forbidden intrusion into free speech.

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:06.040
Now, a Texas appeals court

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.130
concluded that statements

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.308
by Jones and his contributors

00:10:08.308 --> 00:10:10.170
cross the line from hyperbole

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.960
into reckless and defamatory.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.263
And once these defenses were litigated,

00:10:13.263 --> 00:10:14.320
the courts determined

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.500
that the fair reporting privilege

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.460
didn't prevent the plaintiffs

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.278
from suing Jones and Infowars.

00:10:18.278 --> 00:10:19.970
So that meant that the civil suits

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:20.803
could go forward

00:10:20.803 --> 00:10:22.330
and Alex Jones needed to respond

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:23.560
to the discovery requests.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.510
And in July of 2021,

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.590
the plaintiff's lawyers offered

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:27.848
to give Jones and other defendants

00:10:27.848 --> 00:10:29.926
14 more days to answer discovery.

00:10:29.926 --> 00:10:31.170
And they even agreed

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.220
to waive all objections

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.487
to the lateness of the discovery responses

00:10:33.487 --> 00:10:36.570
as long as Jones answered within 14 days.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.470
But the Jones legal team

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:38.399
merely asked for a copy of

00:10:38.399 --> 00:10:39.730
the discovery requests,

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.970
which they were three
years old at that point.

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:42.803
And then they failed

00:10:42.803 --> 00:10:44.300
to make any responses whatsoever.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:45.560
That prompted Pozner's lawyers

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.100
to file a motion to compel discovery

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.029
and for sanctions.

00:10:48.029 --> 00:10:49.250
In the Heslin case,

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.100
the court ordered Jones

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.180
to sit for deposition

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:52.940
and to respond to discovery.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.010
And that was in October of 2019.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:56.290
Jones didn't comply.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.400
So in December,

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:58.720
the court assessed sanctions

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.470
and held Jones in contempt.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.540
And that was back at the time

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.600
that Jones had filed his own

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.380
motion to dismiss under the TCPA

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.540
and the court stayed all
the legal proceedings

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.820
while Jones appealed that TCPA motion.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.530
And Jones promised to supplement

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:11.363
his discovery answers

00:11:11.363 --> 00:11:12.930
as soon as the stay was lifted,

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.310
if the court didn't dismiss the case.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:16.760
However, when the Court of Appeals

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:17.777
did not dismiss the case,

00:11:17.777 --> 00:11:19.300
he didn't do so.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:20.480
In fact, the Jones defendants

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.870
failed to supplement any discovery

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.380
after the stay was lifted.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.410
And a similar pattern

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.440
happened in the Lewis case

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:26.510
where the court ordered Jones

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:27.550
to respond to discovery

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.860
way back in February of 2019.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.430
Jones was supposed to have a deposition

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.600
in March of 2019,

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.947
but instead, nothing happened

00:11:33.947 --> 00:11:35.848
and the proceedings ground to a halt.

00:11:35.848 --> 00:11:37.550
When the judge assessed sanctions

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.383
in the Lewis case,

00:11:38.383 --> 00:11:39.750
Jones offered up some documents,

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:40.972
but each time that happened,

00:11:40.972 --> 00:11:42.900
the documents were not responsive

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.440
to the discovery requests.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:45.273
So what happens

00:11:45.273 --> 00:11:46.330
when you're a plaintiff's attorney

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.390
and the defense just simply refuses

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.140
to respond to your discovery requests?

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.180
Well, under the Texas
Rules of Civil Procedure,

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.650
a litigant may apply for sanctions

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.440
or an order compelling discovery

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.810
when a litigant refuses to agree

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.140
to respond to discovery

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:01.160
or refuses to provide answers.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.461
And motions to compel discovery

00:12:02.461 --> 00:12:05.294
and for sanctions are not rare at all.

00:12:05.294 --> 00:12:06.950
Usually, if they're granted,

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:07.783
they result in the court

00:12:07.783 --> 00:12:08.890
actually compelling the party

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:10.260
to turn over discovery,

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.490
or barring the party resisting discovery

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:14.030
from asserting a certain defense,

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.200
or fining the party

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.350
and maybe getting some attorney's fees

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:19.040
for having to go through the fight.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.270
This happens all the time

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:21.240
because people don't like

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.621
giving up information

00:12:22.621 --> 00:12:24.490
to the other side.

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:25.323
But in this case,

00:12:25.323 --> 00:12:26.700
the court was so exasperated

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.510
by Alex Jones' willful conduct,

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.070
the judge decided to enter

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.968
a default judgment instead.

00:12:31.968 --> 00:12:33.430
Now, a default judgment

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.590
is a binding judgment

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:35.950
in favor of the other party

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:37.019
based on some failure

00:12:37.019 --> 00:12:39.080
to take action by that party.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.020
If this occurs,

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.310
a court might rule in favor

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.390
of the plaintiff by default.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:44.870
Now, it's pretty common for judges

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.070
to enter default judgment

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.550
in cases where a defendant,

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.660
despite being properly served,

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.850
simply never enters an appearance

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.300
or answers the plaintiff's complaint.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.890
That's why, if you're
sued with the lawsuit,

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:55.550
you need to talk to a lawyer

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:57.570
because if you don't respond,

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:59.090
you're going to get a default judgment.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.600
However, here the judge entered

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:01.433
the default judgment

00:13:01.433 --> 00:13:02.266
because the court believed

00:13:02.266 --> 00:13:03.390
that less serious sanctions

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:04.840
would not deter Alex Jones

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.838
from similar actions in the future.

00:13:06.838 --> 00:13:08.707
Quote, "The court rejects lesser sanctions

00:13:08.707 --> 00:13:09.906
"because they've proven ineffective

00:13:09.906 --> 00:13:11.717
"when previously ordered.

00:13:11.717 --> 00:13:13.057
"They would also benefit defendants

00:13:13.057 --> 00:13:15.260
"and increase the cost to plaintiff."

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.210
The court held that Jones

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:17.140
had shown a consistent

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:18.290
pattern of discovery abuse,

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.380
not only on the three related cases,

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.410
but in their other litigation

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.360
pertaining to Sandy Hook in general.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.570
The court also noted that Jones

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.770
had failed to answer discovery

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.039
in defamation case involving Alex Jones'

00:13:27.039 --> 00:13:29.094
statements about a school shooting

00:13:29.094 --> 00:13:30.943
at Marjory Stoneman Douglas
High School in Florida.

00:13:30.943 --> 00:13:31.960
And of course,

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.110
Alex Jones had a right

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:35.570
to file a motion to dismiss the lawsuits.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:37.160
And he had every right to try

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:38.970
to use the TCPA.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:40.190
It wasn't a crazy argument

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.700
to think that the anti-SLAPP laws

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.990
might apply and give him a defense.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.142
But having lost that fight,

00:13:45.142 --> 00:13:47.150
he had a legal responsibility

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.810
to obey the orders of the court

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:50.980
and participate in the discovery process.

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.080
And the lesson to never piss off the judge

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.720
is always a good one.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:55.740
The Texas Court concluded

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.134
that given defendant's bad
faith approach to litigation,

00:13:58.134 --> 00:13:59.860
Mr. Jones' public threats

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.560
and Mr. Jones' professed belief

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.780
that the proceedings are show trials,

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:04.613
that entering a series

00:14:04.613 --> 00:14:05.820
of escalating consequences

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:06.720
would be useless.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.090
So the court entered a default judgment

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:10.910
against Alex Jones.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.460
The court opted not to issue sanctions

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:13.410
against his lawyers.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.430
Noting the Jones had seven lawyers

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.630
during the course of this litigation.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.010
That basically Alex Jones
did whatever he wanted,

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.850
regardless of who was representing him.

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:22.910
So congratulations, Alex Jones.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.030
You played yourself.

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:24.863
And that's not all.

00:14:24.863 --> 00:14:27.250
Now, Alex Jones has lost all 10 lawsuits

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:28.444
brought by families of people killed

00:14:28.444 --> 00:14:29.884
in the Sandy Hook massacre.

00:14:29.884 --> 00:14:31.990
In November, a Connecticut State Court

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:33.050
ruled that because Jones

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.310
disregarded orders requiring him

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.510
to turn over documents,

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:37.030
he's liable by default.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:37.880
The Connecticut judge

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:38.820
used the same logic

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:39.840
as the Texas Court.

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.680
The lead plaintiff in
the Connecticut cases,

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:42.890
Erica Lafferty,

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.500
the daughter of the school principal,

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.190
Dawn Lafferty Hochsprung,

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.663
who was murdered by the same gunman

00:14:47.663 --> 00:14:49.665
as the Sandy Hook children.

00:14:49.665 --> 00:14:50.630
The other plaintiffs

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:51.950
include William Aldenberg,

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:52.880
a first responder

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.050
who Jones has labeled a crisis actor.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:55.990
And when there's a default judgment,

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.150
that doesn't mean the case is over.

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.250
There still has to be a trial

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.500
on the matter of damages.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.920
This is generally called a prove up

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.060
where the winner of the trial

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:05.629
has to demonstrate the actual damages

00:15:05.629 --> 00:15:07.010
that they suffered.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.092
Though, liability is no
longer contested because,

00:15:09.092 --> 00:15:11.550
you know, that was the penalty.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.730
So now, both state courts

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.140
will now schedule a trial

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.881
on how much Jones has to pay.

00:15:15.881 --> 00:15:17.850
Jones has already vowed to appeal

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.900
the Connecticut rulings.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.320
And he also claimed that

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.930
the state courts were
conspiring against him

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.630
to deny him due process.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.097
Quote, "These individuals again

00:15:25.097 --> 00:15:25.930
"you're not allowing me

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:26.763
"to have a jury trial

00:15:26.763 --> 00:15:28.397
"because they know the things they said

00:15:28.397 --> 00:15:30.137
"I supposedly did didn't happen,

00:15:30.137 --> 00:15:32.037
"and they know they didn't have

00:15:32.037 --> 00:15:33.350
"a case for damages."

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.260
So the lesson is,

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.093
if you get sued,

00:15:35.093 --> 00:15:36.400
you should actually participate

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:37.310
in the legal process

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.320
and not obstruct like Alex Jones.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:40.610
And if you do get sued,

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:42.450
call your lawyer immediately.

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.700
And when you make that call,

